                            {
                                "target_word": "blinding",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "62cbfa02-bce2-3d03-8c5b-b28541e09eda",
                                        "entry_id": "78d57591-cbaf-3950-8489-760bc3f71b1d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Very bright (as if to cause blindness)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "91aef17a-3ed1-4fcf-b0d1-8dbe901f91ea",
                                                "sense_id": "62cbfa02-bce2-3d03-8c5b-b28541e09eda",
                                                "text": "On it came, and with it came the glorious blinding cloud of many-coloured light, and stood before us for a space, turning, as it seemed to us, slowly round and round, and then, accompanied by its attendant pomp of sound, passed away I know not whither."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9c23dd11-74a8-39f4-97b2-1ef8fd2f7780",
                                        "entry_id": "78d57591-cbaf-3950-8489-760bc3f71b1d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Making blind or as if blind; depriving of sight or of understanding."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bf4d8dde-8cc7-467f-ac3a-576e98ac8d67",
                                                "sense_id": "9c23dd11-74a8-39f4-97b2-1ef8fd2f7780",
                                                "text": "blinding tears;  blinding snow"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "99f55e4a-fc9d-4132-bdff-bbf126f79738",
                                                "sense_id": "9c23dd11-74a8-39f4-97b2-1ef8fd2f7780",
                                                "text": "Turning back, then, toward the basement staircase, she began to grope her way through blinding darkness, but had taken only a few uncertain steps when, of a sudden, she stopped short and for a little stood like a stricken thing, quite motionless save that she quaked to her very marrow in the grasp of a great and enervating fear."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c509d8de-d743-3713-badb-164a984a5c59",
                                        "entry_id": "78d57591-cbaf-3950-8489-760bc3f71b1d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Brilliant; marvellous."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "UK",
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "85206418-e51e-41dc-a7fc-d7ed01501513",
                                                "sense_id": "c509d8de-d743-3713-badb-164a984a5c59",
                                                "text": "“How’s it going?” “Blinding, mate.”"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "blinding",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fc44b16b-ef64-3df7-b383-82f3503fc722",
                                        "entry_id": "37231e6c-9698-3ac5-8695-fff4de319027",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To an extreme degree; blindingly."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "nonstandard"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8b1347b0-0924-40a6-afbe-88a1a048b17f",
                                                "sense_id": "fc44b16b-ef64-3df7-b383-82f3503fc722",
                                                "text": "certain 'details' of 'scientifically realized socialism' became blinding obvious"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "34657c1e-07a4-49dd-8538-aefa64dfad1c",
                                                "sense_id": "fc44b16b-ef64-3df7-b383-82f3503fc722",
                                                "text": "He made the basket on his second attempt, after an exchange of moves so blinding fast that Derek could barely distinguish them."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8b20d6a2-9462-4370-8922-a7212c59c6d9",
                                                "sense_id": "fc44b16b-ef64-3df7-b383-82f3503fc722",
                                                "text": "I was in a nightmare, and everything was blinding bright, inky black, blinding bright; and fading, and fading"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d65e5dfa-9a1a-47a2-8b83-4a5c0569303d",
                                                "sense_id": "fc44b16b-ef64-3df7-b383-82f3503fc722",
                                                "text": "It's the blinding obvious fact that American football is the real-life equivalent of Quidditch. Or maybe Fireball - the game invented by Joey and Chandler"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bd6f20c4-cba4-48aa-a5ec-4d23c67ae88f",
                                                "sense_id": "fc44b16b-ef64-3df7-b383-82f3503fc722",
                                                "text": "WHILST IT'S blinding obvious that converged networks are the way to go, it's also apparent that C21 [21st Century] networks won't get rapidly rolled out"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5a568599-a7f9-4d69-9cc1-b6f654ccddf4",
                                                "sense_id": "fc44b16b-ef64-3df7-b383-82f3503fc722",
                                                "text": "Roger Yates, chief executive officer of Henderson Group Plc in London, which oversees about $125 billion said Greenspan's remarks were \"blinding obvious\"."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
